[314,697,698],{"class":459}," \u002F\u002F before mount: providers set up earlier aren't seen\n",[314,700,701,703,705,708,710,713],{"class":316,"line":456},[314,702,681],{"class":320},[314,704,684],{"class":364},[314,706,707],{"class":320},"mount",[314,709,670],{"class":364},[314,711,712],{"class":324},"'#app'",[314,714,676],{"class":364},[275,716,717,718,721,722,725,726,729,730,733],{},"Or import ",[278,719,720],{},"@vue-dnd-kit\u002Fdevtools\u002Fauto"," first in the entry file. Use\n",[278,723,724],{},"vueDnDKitDevtools({ inject: false })"," when the plugin should serve the tab but you install the\npage's side yourself; ",[278,727,728],{},"serveTab()"," from ",[278,731,732],{},"@vue-dnd-kit\u002Fdevtools\u002Fvite"," is the middleware that serves\nthe tab.",[735,736,737],"note",{},[275,738,739,740,743,744,747,748,751],{},"In a production build, ",[278,741,742],{},"app.use(DnDDevtools)"," and the ",[278,745,746],{},"auto"," import shrink to almost nothing:\nevery entry point checks ",[278,749,750],{},"process.env.NODE_ENV"," first, and bundlers drop the rest. On the server\nthey do nothing.",[295,753,755],{"id":754},"open-it","Open it",[757,758,759,781,796],"ul",{},[760,761,762,765,766,770,771,770,774,777,778,780],"li",{},[283,763,764],{},"Vue DevTools",": ",[767,768],"kbd",{"value":769},"Alt"," + ",[767,772],{"value":773},"Shift",[767,775],{"value":776},"D",", or the Vue button at\nthe bottom of the page, then the ",[283,779,285],{}," tab.",[760,782,783,765,786,770,788,770,790,792,793,795],{},[283,784,785],{},"Nuxt DevTools",[767,787],{"value":769},[767,789],{"value":773},[767,791],{"value":776},", or the Nuxt button,\nthen ",[283,794,285],{}," (in the sidebar or its overflow menu).",[760,797,798,801,802,805],{},[283,799,800],{},"A window of its own",": open ",[278,803,804],{},"http:\u002F\u002Flocalhost:5173\u002F__vue-dnd-kit-devtools\u002F"," on your dev server,\nor the tab's ⧉ button. Handy on a second screen. With several pages open, a select on top\nchooses the one to watch.",[807,808,809],"warning",{},[275,810,811],{},"Keep the tab in a window of its own, not in a background browser tab of the same window: the page\nmust stay visible, and a hidden page cancels drags.",[295,813,815],{"id":814},"the-tab-at-a-glance","The tab at a glance",[817,818,819,832],"table",{},[820,821,822],"thead",{},[823,824,825,829],"tr",{},[826,827,828],"th",{},"Part",[826,830,831],{},"What it holds",[833,834,835,852,864,879],"tbody",{},[823,836,837,841],{},[838,839,840],"td",{},"Top bar",[838,842,843,844,847,848,851],{},"What the drag is doing right now (",[278,845,846],{},"dragging card-3 → done (accepts)","), the page watched, ",[283,849,850],{},"⌖ Pick",", the count of edited options with a reset, ⧉ (a window of its own) and the theme.",[823,853,854,857],{},[838,855,856],{},"Left: the registry",[838,858,859,860,863],{},"Every provider as a tree: its lists, trees, drop targets and draggables. ",[283,861,862],{},"☰"," shows or hides it.",[823,865,866,876],{},[838,867,868,869,872,873],{},"Middle: ",[283,870,871],{},"Map"," and ",[283,874,875],{},"Log",[838,877,878],{},"The live mini-map of the page, or the log of the drags.",[823,880,881,893],{},[838,882,883,884,578,887,578,890],{},"Right: ",[283,885,886],{},"Drive",[283,888,889],{},"Options",[283,891,892],{},"State",[838,894,895],{},"The joystick and the move buttons, the options of the chosen node, and what the provider knows about it.",[275,897,898],{},"Choose a node in the registry or an item on the map, and the right side follows it.",[295,900,902],{"id":901},"the-mini-map","The mini-map",[275,904,905],{},"A live card per list, tree and drop target, with copies of their items where they are — the same\nclones the overlay would show, with the page's CSS. During a drag it marks:",[757,907,908,919,922],{},[760,909,910,911,914,915,918],{},"the lists and targets that ",[283,912,913],{},"accept"," the drag (blue) or ",[283,916,917],{},"refuse"," it (red);",[760,920,921],{},"the placeholder, and the target under the pointer;",[760,923,924,925,928],{},"the pointer, the overlay's box, and the insertion line of ",[278,926,927],{},"placeholder: 'indicator'"," lists.",[275,930,931],{},"A click chooses an item and highlights it on the page; a double click scrolls the page to it. Use\nthe map when a drop doesn't go where you expect: it shows at a glance which lists take the drag.",[295,933,935],{"id":934},"drive-the-joystick","Drive: the joystick",[275,937,938,939,941,942,872,945,948],{},"Choose an item — on the map, in the registry, or with ",[283,940,850],{},", which takes the next press on a\ndraggable of the page instead of letting it act — and push the joystick's knob. The item is picked\nup and moves that way, faster the farther the knob is from the center. Let go and it stops;\n",[283,943,944],{},"Drop",[283,946,947],{},"Cancel"," end the drag.",[275,950,951,952,955,956,961,962,872,965,968],{},"It is a real pointer drag of a sensor named ",[278,953,954],{},"devtools",", made with the public\n",[957,958,960],"a",{"href":959},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fguides\u002Fsensors#a-sensor-of-your-own","sensor API",": lists sort under it, containers\nauto-scroll at their edges, and ",[278,963,964],{},"onBeforeDrop",[278,966,967],{},"onDrop"," run as for any drag. Disabled items\naren't picked up. A keyboard drag the page started can be steered too.",[275,970,971,972,978],{},"Items of sortable lists also get buttons: up, down, to the start, to the end, to another list of\nthe group. Each is one keyboard drag of ",[957,973,975],{"href":974},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fguides\u002Fsensors#programmatic-drags",[278,976,977],{},"moveItem",".\nBelow the joystick, a large copy of what the overlay shows.",[817,980,981,991],{},[820,982,983],{},[823,984,985,988],{},[826,986,987],{},"Key, in the tab",[826,989,990],{},"Does",[833,992,993,1016,1026,1039,1048],{},[823,994,995,1010],{},[838,996,997,998,1001,1002,1001,1005,1001,1008],{},"Arrows or ",[767,999],{"value":1000},"W"," ",[767,1003],{"value":1004},"A",[767,1006],{"value":1007},"S",[767,1009],{"value":776},[838,1011,1012,1013,1015],{},"Push the knob that way, halfway; with ",[767,1014],{"value":773},", all the way",[823,1017,1018,1023],{},[838,1019,1020],{},[767,1021],{"value":1022},"G",[838,1024,1025],{},"Pick the chosen item up",[823,1027,1028,1037],{},[838,1029,1030,1033,1034],{},[767,1031],{"value":1032},"Space"," \u002F ",[767,1035],{"value":1036},"Enter",[838,1038,944],{},[823,1040,1041,1046],{},[838,1042,1043],{},[767,1044],{"value":1045},"Escape",[838,1047,947],{},[823,1049,1050,1055],{},[838,1051,1052],{},[767,1053],{"value":1054},"P",[838,1056,1057],{},"Pick on the page",[295,1059,889],{"id":1060},"options",[275,1062,1063,1064,470],{},"Every option that isn't a callback can be edited while the app runs. Choose the node and open\n",[283,1065,889],{},[817,1067,1068,1077],{},[820,1069,1070],{},[823,1071,1072,1075],{},[826,1073,1074],{},"Node",[826,1076,889],{},[833,1078,1079,1121,1160,1178,1194],{},[823,1080,1081,1084],{},[838,1082,1083],{},"Provider",[838,1085,1086,578,1089,578,1092,578,1095,1098,1099,578,1102,578,1105,578,1108,578,1111,578,1114,578,1117,1120],{},[278,1087,1088],{},"overlayFit",[278,1090,1091],{},"autoScroll",[278,1093,1094],{},"collision",[278,1096,1097],{},"modifiers"," (the library's, by name), ",[278,1100,1101],{},"animation",[278,1103,1104],{},"dropAnimation",[278,1106,1107],{},"animateChanges",[278,1109,1110],{},"activation",[278,1112,1113],{},"keyboard",[278,1115,1116],{},"haptics",[278,1118,1119],{},"copyModifier","…",[823,1122,1123,1126],{},[838,1124,1125],{},"List",[838,1127,1128,578,1131,578,1134,578,1137,578,1140,578,1143,578,1146,578,1149,578,1152,578,1154,578,1156,578,1158],{},[278,1129,1130],{},"disabled",[278,1132,1133],{},"strategy",[278,1135,1136],{},"placeholder",[278,1138,1139],{},"behavior",[278,1141,1142],{},"multiple",[278,1144,1145],{},"sort",[278,1147,1148],{},"dropOutside",[278,1150,1151],{},"acceptMode",[278,1153,1101],{},[278,1155,1107],{},[278,1157,1091],{},[278,1159,1097],{},[823,1161,1162,1165],{},[838,1163,1164],{},"Tree",[838,1166,1167,578,1169,578,1172,578,1175,1120],{},[278,1168,1136],{},[278,1170,1171],{},"indentation",[278,1173,1174],{},"nesting",[278,1176,1177],{},"maxDepth",[823,1179,1180,1183],{},[838,1181,1182],{},"Drop target",[838,1184,1185,578,1187,578,1190,578,1192],{},[278,1186,1130],{},[278,1188,1189],{},"priority",[278,1191,913],{},[278,1193,1151],{},[823,1195,1196,1199],{},[838,1197,1198],{},"Item",[838,1200,1201,578,1203,578,1206],{},[278,1202,1130],{},[278,1204,1205],{},"keyboardMode",[278,1207,1110],{},[275,1209,1210],{},"An edit applies at once, to this page only, and is never written to your code: the library reads\nthe new value where it reads the option. It lasts until you reset it (↺ per option, or the reset in\nthe top bar), the provider unmounts or the page reloads. An edited option shows your code's value\nnext to it. Items mounted while an edit is set — rows of a virtual list — get it too.",[295,1212,892],{"id":1213},"state",[275,1215,1216],{},"What each provider knows, for the node you chose:",[757,1218,1219,1226,1237],{},[760,1220,1221,1222,1225],{},"the ",[283,1223,1224],{},"drag session",": status, the active ids, items and sensor, the target and whether it\naccepts, the pointer, the overlay, the sortable group's session and insertion line;",[760,1227,1228,1229,1232,1233,1236],{},"a ",[283,1230,1231],{},"list",": its order and its draft; a ",[283,1234,1235],{},"tree",": its rows;",[760,1238,1239,1240,1243,1244,1247],{},"an ",[283,1241,1242],{},"item",": its type, data and position; a ",[283,1245,1246],{},"drop target",": its rules.",[275,1249,1250],{},"Items mount and unmount without events: the registry catches up within a second.",[295,1252,875],{"id":1253},"log",[275,1255,1256],{},"One band per drag, in order:",[817,1258,1259,1269],{},[820,1260,1261],{},[823,1262,1263,1266],{},[826,1264,1265],{},"Entry",[826,1267,1268],{},"What it tells",[833,1270,1271,1281,1294,1307,1319,1337],{},[823,1272,1273,1278],{},[838,1274,1275],{},[278,1276,1277],{},"drag start",[838,1279,1280],{},"The ids, the sensor and whether by touch, the list it comes from.",[823,1282,1283,1291],{},[838,1284,1285,578,1288],{},[278,1286,1287],{},"over",[278,1289,1290],{},"left",[838,1292,1293],{},"Each target entered and left, and whether it accepts.",[823,1295,1296,1301],{},[838,1297,1298],{},[278,1299,1300],{},"release",[838,1302,1303,1304,1306],{},"The target it was let go on, while ",[278,1305,964],{}," decides.",[823,1308,1309,1313],{},[838,1310,1311],{},[278,1312,964],{},[838,1314,1315,1316,1318],{},"The verdict: accepted, some accepted, rejected by a hook, refused by the target's ",[278,1317,913],{},", and how long the hooks took.",[823,1320,1321,1326],{},[838,1322,1323],{},[278,1324,1325],{},"drop",[838,1327,1328,1329,1332,1333,1336],{},"The target; for sortable lists the move, ",[278,1330,1331],{},"e.result",", and whether ",[278,1334,1335],{},"preventDefault()"," was called.",[823,1338,1339,1344],{},[838,1340,1341],{},[278,1342,1343],{},"cancel",[838,1345,1346,1347,1350,1351,684],{},"Why: cancelled (Escape, ",[278,1348,1349],{},"cancel()","), rejected by a hook, or refused by the target's ",[278,1352,913],{},[275,1354,1355,1356,872,1359,1362,1363,1366,1367,1370],{},"Also ",[278,1357,1358],{},"auto-scroll on",[278,1360,1361],{},"off",", the ",[278,1364,1365],{},"announcement"," texts (hidden by default) and, outside drags,\n",[278,1368,1369],{},"animate"," (changes of a list's items that no drag made). Click an entry for its data. A tab that\nopens later gets the drags so far.",[295,1372,1374],{"id":1373},"debug-a-drop-step-by-step","Debug a drop, step by step",[275,1376,1377],{},"A card won't go into a column. With the tab open:",[1379,1380,1381,1390,1407,1428],"ol",{},[760,1382,1383,1386,1387,1389],{},[283,1384,1385],{},"Reproduce it"," by hand, or with ",[283,1388,886],{}," so your hands stay free for the tab.",[760,1391,1392,1395,1396,1399,1400,1403,1404,1406],{},[283,1393,1394],{},"Watch the map"," while the card is over the column. Red means the list refuses the card: look at\nits ",[278,1397,1398],{},"group"," (",[278,1401,1402],{},"put",") or the target's ",[278,1405,913],{},". Blue means it accepts, and the problem comes later.",[760,1408,1409,1412,1413,1415,1416,1418,1419,1421,1422,1424,1425,1427],{},[283,1410,1411],{},"Read the log"," of that drag. ",[278,1414,964],{}," says who said no — a hook, or the target's\n",[278,1417,913],{},". If the drop went through but your data didn't change, the ",[278,1420,1325],{}," entry says whether\n",[278,1423,1335],{}," was called and what ",[278,1426,1331],{}," held: a controlled list must apply it itself.",[760,1429,1430,1433,1434,1436,1437,1439,1440,578,1442,1444],{},[283,1431,1432],{},"Try a fix live"," in ",[283,1435,889],{}," — a looser ",[278,1438,1151],{},", another ",[278,1441,1094],{},[278,1443,927],{}," — then write the one that works into your code.",[295,1446,1448],{"id":1447},"how-it-works","How it works",[275,1450,1451,1452,1455],{},"Providers report to a hook that the page's side installs. Until a tab watches the page, they are\nonly recorded; then the page listens like any monitor and sends the tab what it shows — every\n40 ms during a drag, twice a second otherwise — and stops once no tab has watched for a few\nseconds. The tab talks to the page over a ",[278,1453,1454],{},"BroadcastChannel"," of the page's origin. It changes\nnothing but what you ask for: the drags, the selection and the option overrides.",[1457,1458,1459],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sbwC8, html code.shiki .sbwC8{--shiki-light:#0969DA;--shiki-default:#0969DA;--shiki-dark:#7CC4FF}html pre.shiki code .sN8r7, html code.shiki .sN8r7{--shiki-light:#9A6700;--shiki-default:#9A6700;--shiki-dark:#E9C46A}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(-